149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (While unfairness is not something we strive for, I think we can all agree that it is something that helps us grow. Facing and overcoming unfairness allows us to adapt and become stronger. Life would feel stagnant without challenges, as growth, evolution, and development often come from adversity. Just as you cannot see the beautiful stars without the darkness of space, you cannot experience genuine triumph without the possibility of unfair loss. Unfairness creates opportunities for virtue, choice, and compassion. We show kindness, offer help, and give to those in need because life is not fair to everyone. If there were no unfairness, helping others would become unnecessary or even impossible. True kindness has meaning precisely because the world is not always fair.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
